 "answer": "Whether you should keep your kids home depends on their health sensitivity and whether they have weekend classes or you are planning for Monday. Under the latest guidelines from the Ministry of Education (MOE), **you are officially permitted to keep your children home due to the haze, provided you inform the school.**\n\n### 1. Current Air Quality in Kuala Lumpur\n* **Current Reading:** KL’s official Air Pollutant Index (API) at both the **Batu Muda** and **Cheras** stations is hovering around **164** (with surrounding Selangor and Putrajaya areas between **165 and 171**).\n* **Status:** **Unhealthy (API 101–200)**. At this level, anyone can experience mild irritation (coughing, throat irritation, watery eyes), and children with asthma or respiratory conditions are at higher risk.\n\n### 2. Latest Ministry of Education (MOE) Guidelines\nFollowing the policy update by Education Minister Fadhlina Sidek, the MOE reverted to the National Haze Action Plan (PTJK) thresholds:\n* **API > 100 (Current level in KL):** Schools remain open, but **all outdoor activities and physical education classes must be suspended.**\n* **API > 200:** Mandatory school closures and a shift to home-based teaching and learning (PdPR).\n* **Parental Discretion:** The MOE explicitly allows parents to keep their children at home if they are worried about health risks—even if the API is below 200—as long as you **notify the school administration/class teacher in advance**.\n\n### 3. Should They Stay Home?\n* **Keep them home if:**\n  * Your children have asthma, allergies, bronchitis, or any underlying respiratory/heart conditions.\n  * Their school has open-air classrooms without air conditioning or air purifiers, or their commute involves walking or waiting outdoors.\n  * They are already showing symptoms like coughing, sore throat, or eye irritation.\n* **If they do attend school (or weekend co-curriculars):**\n  * Send them with a well-fitted **N95 or KN95 mask** (standard surgical or cloth masks do not effectively filter fine PM2.5 haze particles).\n  * Pack extra **clean drinking water** so they stay well-hydrated throughout the day.\n  * Confirm with the school that all sports and outdoor assemblies have been moved indoors.\n\n*(Note: Check the official **DOE MyIPU app** or the **APIMS website** (`apims.doe.gov.my`) on the morning of their next school day, as readings and district-level school closure notices—especially in neighboring Selangor districts—can change overnight.)*",
